# Branch + PR workflow

Never commit feature work directly on `master`. For every change set in this repo:

1. **Branch first** — create and switch to a new branch from up-to-date `master` before editing (e.g. `feat/theme-toggle`, `fix/mobile-layout`).
2. **Commit on the branch** — only when the user asks to commit; keep commits scoped to that task.
3. **Open a PR into `master`** — push with `-u` and create a PR targeting `master` (use `gh pr create`). Do not merge unless the user explicitly asks.
4. **One concern per PR** — do not mix unrelated features (e.g. theme + mobile) in the same branch/PR.
5. **Stay off master** — if already on `master` with uncommitted work, create a branch before committing; never push straight to `master` for app changes.

```bash
# ✅ typical flow
git checkout master && git pull
git checkout -b feat/short-description
# ... work ...
git push -u origin HEAD
gh pr create --base master --title "..." --body "..."

# ❌ avoid
git checkout master
# edit + commit + push to master
```
